  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>everolimus</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L01EG02</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, IV dosing <small>(PK_2C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Hirabatake M et al. 2022</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>Japanese patients with advanced breast cancer</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>everolimus</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_everolimus/Everolimus_Hirabatake2022_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>CL (L/h/70 kg)</td><td>11.7</td><td>L/h/70 kg</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>V1 (L/70 kg)</td><td>54.0</td><td>L/70 kg</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>Q (L/h/70 kg)</td><td>42.2</td><td>L/h/70 kg</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr><tr><td>V2 (L/70 kg)</td><td>309.4</td><td>L/70 kg</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr></table><h4>About everolimus</h4><p>Everolimus is an mTOR inhibitor used as an antineoplastic and immunosuppressant for cancers such as renal cell carcinoma, breast cancer, and neuroendocrine tumors, as well as tuberous sclerosis. It is authorised in the European Union for several cancer types and tuberous sclerosis, and is an approved drug.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q421052\">Wikidata Q421052</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Everolimus\">Everolimus</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Hirabatake M et al. (2022). Everolimus pharmacokinetics and exposure-response relationship in Japanese patients with advanced breast cancer. <i>Frontiers in pharmacology 13:984002</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3389/fphar.2022.984002\">10.3389/fphar.2022.984002</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36188563\">36188563</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Hirabatake_2022: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
